# Content URL prefixes (new pages only)

Do not invent a new top-level prefix. Do not move or 301 existing URLs unless the user explicitly asks.

## New editorial (artigo / guia)

Always `/blog/:slug` via `guide.js` + `data/guide/`. Listing: `/blog`. Magazine index: `/magazine` (not a per-article prefix). `/guide/:slug` only redirects to `/blog/:slug`.

```
# good — new guide
/blog/sono-e-burnout-em-enfermeiros

# bad — new article under a product prefix
/burnout/sono-e-enfermeiros
/nutricao/guia-proteina
/wellness/artigo-termas
```

## Product / category prefixes (not magazine articles)

Keep these for hubs, tools, and service/condition/directory fichas. Do not add new editorial slugs here.

| Prefix | Role |
|---|---|
| `/burnout` | Hub + existing spokes. Quiz: `/burnout/teste`. No new article spokes. |
| `/nutricao/:slug` | Nutrition service/condition pages |
| `/wellness/:slug` | Experience fichas |
| `/consulta/:slug` | Medical complaint conversion |
| `/:slug` at root | Psychology queixas and tourist GEO landings (existing pattern) |

New burnout writing that is an article goes to `/blog/` and links to `/burnout`. Existing `/burnout/:slug` pages stay as they are.
